The Windermere Children is a 2020 British biographical drama television
film written by Simon Block and directed by Michael Samuels.

10
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Based on the experience of child survivors of the Holocaust, it follows the children and staff of a camp set up on the Calgarth Estate  in Troutbeck Bridge,
near Lake Windermere, England, where the survivors were helped to rehabilitate, rebuild their lives, and integrate into the British society.

11
01:04:32,000 --> 01:04:38,000
The film was produced by Simon Block as 'executive producer' with Nancy
Bornat as factual producer and Ben Evans as development producer.

12
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
The film first aired on BBC Two in January 2020.

13
01:16:16,000 --> 01:16:22,000
The film explores themes of childhood trauma, based on true story,
holocaust (shoah) survivor, kindness, compassion.

